hnical (+5%), W.P. (any except heavy weapons, stored as except W.P. Heavy Military Weapons and W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons) and Wilderness (+5%). The book prints Rogue, Technical (+5%); the +5% is read as Technical''s only. SECONDARY: printed select two at levels 2, 6, 8 and 12, read as none at level one and two at each of those levels (count 0 with a schedule). || EQUIPMENT (printed 184): stored where a catalog row exists: pocket knife, Vibro-Knife, a couple of small sacks (2), backpack (the book says backpack or satchel), canteen (or waterskin), pocket mirror, silver cross (Small Silver Cross) and tinted goggles (Sunglasses or Goggles, cheap). Not stored, no catalog rows and not stubbed: one weapon and an extra ammo clip per W.P., a bag of hats, colorful scarves, 1D4 sets of gloves, oversized boots, clothing, a set of light partial armor (2D6+20 M.D.C.), 1D4 tubes of lipstick, an inflatable beach ball, 1D4+4 juggling balls, a shoulder bag of 2D4+2 lbs of candy, a jar of honey, a box of 100 tea bags, a spoon, a teapot, 1D4+2 plastic teacups, a comb and personal items; these are in GM Notes. || MONEY: 3D4x100 Universal Credits. || NOT STORED: size 4 feet (up to 12 by shape change), weight 60-100 lbs, life span 2D6+40 (+20 urban), slave market value 6D6x100, habitat, allies and enemies are in GM Notes."
